Flayr Tune patch for JUCE 8.0.16-security (ea77444750de45e036e0279bb0291144bf8e3688).

State checks in the AU and LV2 wrappers, which handle a project's state before
the plug-in does:
  * AU RestoreState: the class-info property list must be a CFDictionary
    (it was copied as one unchecked), and the "jucePluginState" value must be
    CFData no larger than INT_MAX (any other CF type was read as CFData).
  * LV2 retrieve: if the base64 session state doesn't decode (see
    juce-base64-declared-size.patch), or decodes to more than INT_MAX bytes,
    report an error instead of passing a truncated size on.

Applied by CMakeLists.txt via FetchContent PATCH_COMMAND.

Flayr-Patch-Marker: modules/juce_audio_plugin_client/juce_audio_plugin_client_AU_1.mm FLAYR_PATCH juce-wrapper-state-checks
Flayr-Patch-Marker: modules/juce_audio_plugin_client/juce_audio_plugin_client_LV2.cpp FLAYR_PATCH juce-wrapper-state-checks

diff --git a/modules/juce_audio_plugin_client/juce_audio_plugin_client_AU_1.mm b/modules/juce_audio_plugin_client/juce_audio_plugin_client_AU_1.mm
index 68c8f3c09e..34d1080947 100644
--- a/modules/juce_audio_plugin_client/juce_audio_plugin_client_AU_1.mm
+++ b/modules/juce_audio_plugin_client/juce_audio_plugin_client_AU_1.mm
@@ -868,6 +868,10 @@ ComponentResult RestoreState (CFPropertyListRef inData) override
     {
         const ScopedValueSetter<bool> scope { restoringState, true };
 
+        // FLAYR_PATCH juce-wrapper-state-checks: the state comes from a project file; don't assume its types.
+        if (inData == nullptr || CFGetTypeID (inData) != CFDictionaryGetTypeID())
+            return kAudioUnitErr_InvalidPropertyValue;
+
         {
             // Remove the data entry from the state to prevent the superclass loading the parameters
             CFUniquePtr<CFMutableDictionaryRef> copyWithoutData (CFDictionaryCreateMutableCopy (nullptr, 0, (CFDictionaryRef) inData));
@@ -910,7 +914,9 @@ ComponentResult RestoreState (CFPropertyListRef inData) override
 
             if (valuePresent)
             {
-                if (data != nullptr)
+                // Flayr patch: only CFData, and only sizes an int can hold.
+                if (data != nullptr && CFGetTypeID (data) == CFDataGetTypeID()
+                    && CFDataGetLength (data) <= (CFIndex) std::numeric_limits<int>::max())
                 {
                     const int numBytes = (int) CFDataGetLength (data);
                     const juce::uint8* const rawBytes = CFDataGetBytePtr (data);
diff --git a/modules/juce_audio_plugin_client/juce_audio_plugin_client_LV2.cpp b/modules/juce_audio_plugin_client/juce_audio_plugin_client_LV2.cpp
